# Default settings for earlyoom. This file is sourced by /bin/sh from
# /etc/init.d/earlyoom or by systemd from earlyoom.service.

# Options to pass to earlyoom
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600"

# Examples:

# Print memory report every minute instead of every hour
# EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 60"

# Available minimum memory 5%
# EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 5"

# Available minimum memory 15% and free minimum swap 5%
# EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 15 -s 5"

# Avoid killing processes whose name matches the following regexp.
#
# Do NOT quote the regexp. earlyoom.service uses
#     ExecStart=/usr/bin/earlyoom $EARLYOOM_ARGS
# and systemd splits $EARLYOOM_ARGS on whitespace WITHOUT performing shell
# quote removal, so any quotes you add arrive as literal characters and the
# regexp then matches nothing. For the same reason the regexp must not contain
# a literal space; use the POSIX character class [[:space:]] where you need one,
# e.g. Isolated[[:space:]]Web[[:space:]]Co to match Firefox's "Isolated Web Co".
# EARLYOOM_ARGS="--avoid (^|/)(init|X|sshd|firefox)$"

# See more at `earlyoom -h'
